# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Docker Registry v2 with NO authentication on :5000
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the unauthenticated registry is ALREADY SERVING when the agent starts (a
#     do-nothing agent must fail: unauthenticated GET /v2/_catalog returns 200);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the registry cannot kill the box.
#
# The registry reads its auth settings (REGISTRY_AUTH*) from the environment at
# process start, so the fix must RESTART the registry with those variables set —
# editing config without restarting leaves the running registry open, which the
# verifier detects by hitting the LIVE /v2/_catalog endpoint.
